# Unanchored so it covers build directories of nested crates that carry their
# own workspace, not just the root one. Their artifacts embed absolute paths
# from the machine that built them, which is a disclosure in a public
# repository; an anchored rule left every nested crate to be named by hand.
target/
bench/results/
bench/data/*.jsonl

# Keep internal records and tool state local; publishable guidance and release
# inputs remain trackable through the explicit exceptions below.
# CortexKit layout: see WORKSPACE.md "Where files go"
/.cortexkit/*
!/.cortexkit/release-notes/
!/.cortexkit/skills/
!/.cortexkit/rules/
!/.cortexkit/WORKER.md
# Anchored to the top level on purpose: this excludes the operator's calibration
# records and certification policies, NOT docs/evidence, which is published
# measurement evidence and is tracked. An unanchored rule matches at any depth,
# which silently ignored every new file under docs/evidence while the files
# already committed there kept working, since tracking beats ignoring.
/evidence/
operations/
corpus/aft-chunks.jsonl
.banlist.local
tools/classify-distill/

# Python bytecode from running the reference generator and its tests.
__pycache__/
